WEBVTT

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.510
"EPISODE 12
THE PRETTY BOY ON D HILL (PART 3)"

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.890
Are you saying a classmate
almost killed her?

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:23.390
By her rival candidate Yokuya?

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.560
Though the guy who tried
to run over Mayumi

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.440
and the guy who ran over Naganawa
might not be the same guy.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.900
I don't know about that.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:37.740
I don't think there'd be many people wanting to
intentionally run over middle school kids.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.080
Maybe it was just to threaten her?

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.790
Perhaps they didn't intend on running over her,
but wanted to just intimidate Miss Mayumi.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.670
He was looking away.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.880
Looking away?

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.630
Yes, looking away.

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:57.430
Yokuya, at that crucial moment, wasn't looking
straight ahead, but was looking elsewhere.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:00.970
In other words, he didn't do it on purpose,

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:05.940
but since he was looking away while driving,
he almost plowed into you two?

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.060
That moment when
he was about to run over me,

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.650
when he was about to run over a human,

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:14.110
he held the steering wheel in one hand,

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.950
and fiddled on his smartphone with the other.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.330
It didn't feel like distracted driving.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:23.290
It felt more like
the driving was the incidental part.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:28.670
He was just trying to run over me
in his spare time and with an arm to spare, too.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.710
I'm really scared.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:36.880
I'm scared of cars to the point where
I never want to walk along a road again,

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.850
but more than that, I'm afraid of Yokuya.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.770
I don't want anything to do with him at all.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.770
I don't just want to get my seat reassigned,
but I want to go to another class.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.730
No, I even want to transfer schools.
That's how terrified I feel.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:59.070
But I have to go against such an un-individualistic
person as my rival in an election.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.080
Mayumi.

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:04.910
Maybe we should call it quits.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.670
You really might get murdered next time.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.960
Your resolution and effort have been beautiful,

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.720
but this shouldn't be something
to risk your life over.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.340
Because this is...

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.100
...child's play, after all.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:32.360
Indeed.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.860
Even if it wasn't intimidation,
it's still a threat.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:40.950
If you withdraw your candidacy now,
I'm sure no further harm will come to you.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.540
Yeah. If we're going to debate against
the academy about their curriculum's direction,

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.660
it's not like there aren't other methods.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:53.090
Right. They say
"when there's life, there's hope."

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.460
Adventures are only tolerated
up to kidnappings.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.680
When it goes all the way to murder,
it gets a little too...

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:25.450
No, I won't quit!

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.950
I'll never quit!

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.290
This is merely child's play.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.130
That's why I can't stop at this point.

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.420
Indeed. But, Mayumi—

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:40.470
If I stop here, it's not beautiful, it's not
being a boy, and it's not being a detective.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.340
And most of all, it's not us, a team.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.510
I couldn't stand it.

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.730
I couldn't accept the phrase

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:55.520
"Maybe we should call it quits."
coming out from Manabu Sotoin's mouth.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.530
Because of me, for my sake,

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:04.110
Mr. Delinquent, Mr. Senpai,
Mr. Bare-Legs, and Mr. Genius

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:07.160
were putting up with the
leader's comments.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:08.910
I can't ever tolerate that.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:16.380
Of course, someday we'll graduate,
and "child's play" will come to an end.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.590
But now is not that time yet.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:25.760
What are you if you mature because
you submitted to a shabby hit-and-run crook?

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.430
Manabu the Aesthete
should not be learning from defeat.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:34.390
If you're going to learn,
learn from beauty. Isn't that right?

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.480
Not common knowledge, not common sense,

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.730
but a sense of aestheticism.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.190
Isn't that right, Leader?

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.700
I have absolutely no intention of risking my life
for the academy's so-called principle operations.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:55.830
But I'm not here in this art room so
that disgusting pretty boys can protect me.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:05:01.630
I'm not a princess. I'm a Pretty Boy, too.

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:09.180
Oh brother. That was
a terrible slip of the tongue on my part.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:14.350
Before we knew it, you've become an established
member of the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.810
You're no longer an apprentice Pretty Boy.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.400
"APPRENTICE" "ESTABLISHED"

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.400
Huh? I was still an apprentice?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:23.280
Well then, Mayumi and my fellow members!

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.610
I will retract my previous statement,
and correct it!

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:32.580
Let's kick it up a notch.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.750
"SLEEPOVER ELECTION"

00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:11.430
Until the actual day of the election,
Mayumi can simply sleep over in this art room.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:15.060
What's lacking is, let's see,
a bathtub made of cypress?

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.060
Sosaku, can you get one ready by later today?

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.390
If it's for Mayu.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.020
Whoa, he just spoke normally.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:24.520
W-Wait, Sosaku calls you "Mayu"?

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:27.900
B-Before that, you said sleep over right here?

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:31.990
W-Well, there's a bed,
and there's a personal chef.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:37.830
If you want that personal chef to be working,
let's debate a bit more about your nickname.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:39.370
Right, "Mayu"?

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:44.750
B-But Mr. Genius,
can you really make a bathtub?

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:48.170
What is this? This really feels like us now.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.840
It's really feeling like
the Pretty Boy Detective Club.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:56.100
As someone on an athletic team, if we built
a bath here, it'd make my life a lot easier.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.310
Though, I'd be okay with just a footbath, too.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.640
That's so like him.

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.730
I can procure some space
over in the prep room.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:05.480
You can feel at ease.

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:09.860
I was thinking Mayu's body
still had room for a bit more polishing.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.820
Hold on a second, Mr. Genius.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.820
Are you saying that
you're going to be bathing with me?

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:17.280
Then it's decided.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:21.210
This will secure Mayumi's safety
for the time being.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:25.460
Now, we should continue the support
we've been giving thus far...

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.670
to our next student council president!

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:34.590
"FIRST PLACE --MAYUMI DOJIMA
SECOND PLACE --KINSHIRO YOKUYA"

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:37.050
"ELECTION DAY"

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:43.140
"YUBIWA MIDDLE SCHOOL ACADEMY
STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION"
It may seem a bit late,

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:47.440
"YUBIWA MIDDLE SCHOOL ACADEMY
STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION"
but let me introduce you to the election
system at Yubiwa Academy Middle School.

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:51.530
After listening to the speeches
of the recommenders and the nominees,

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:56.110
you write down the name of the person
you approve of, and drop it into the ballot box.

00:08:56.110 --> 00:09:01.500
By the way, the speeches are conducted
by year, class, and attendance number order.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:01.950
"CLASS 2-A"

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.330
"CLASS 2-A"
"TOSEN ITSUTSUKI"

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.330
Starting with candidates from Class 2-A,
I'm second from last as someone from Class 2-B.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.870
"CLASS 2-A"
"MUGI OTSUMUGI"

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.870
Starting with candidates from Class 2-A,
I'm second from last as someone from Class 2-B.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.080
"CLASS 2-A"
"KYUYA HITOU"

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.080
Starting with candidates from Class 2-A,
I'm second from last as someone from Class 2-B.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:06.790
Starting with candidates from Class 2-A,
I'm second from last as someone from Class 2-B.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:07.540
"CLASS 2-B"

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.840
"CLASS 2-B"
"MAYUMI DOJIMA"

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.840
The final speaker will be Yokuya,
who is also from 2-B.

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.460
"CLASS 2-B"
"KINSHIRO YOKUYA"

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.460
The final speaker will be Yokuya,
who is also from 2-B.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.970
Of course, my endorsement speech
will be conducted

00:09:15.970 --> 00:09:20.140
by the current student council president,
Nagahiro Sakiguchi.

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.270
Along with that master of speeches,

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.520
and my approval ratings that were first
in preliminary polls, my victory should be set.

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.810
Ladies and gentlemen, lend an ear!

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:32.230
My speech that follows it will be dead rubber.

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:38.530
But the problem is that after our speeches,
it's Yokuya's speech.

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.780
"STUDENT COUNCIL
PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE SPEECH"

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:40.780
Thank you, I am Mugi Osode, Class 2-A.
The reason why I decided to volunteer this year

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.370
That's right.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:47.960
I hadn't really thought about why Yokuya
became the top candidate after Naganawa retired.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.880
is because I wanted to create a school

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.880
Why wasn't the person another candidate
from class A, but it was Yokuya?

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.720
where all students are cheerful and energetic,
and can concentrate further in their studies.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:57.260
Why couldn't any of the other candidates grasp
the students' hearts as much as Yokuya could?

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.010
There's this popular saying...

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:04.850
If Naganawa was targeted
so she would withdraw from the election,

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.100
and if I was targeted for the same reason,

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.690
then why weren't
the other candidates targeted?

00:10:12.690 --> 00:10:16.700
Why didn't Yokuya pay any
attention to them?

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:20.700
--Why didn't those people fall prey to Yokuya?
--...fall prey to Yokuya?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:25.040
Is that what you were
wondering about right now?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:31.590
I didn't run the others over
because it was too cumbersome to do so.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:34.840
It's not my hobby
to enjoy running over people.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:37.220
There was meaning to running over Naganawa,

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:40.390
and there was meaning
to run over you, too, Dojima.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:43.680
And that's as long as the current
student council president has your back.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:48.560
But the others who don't have that will just
lose the election, even if I left them alone.

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:53.690
By the way, it seems you guys
were thoroughly investigating D Hill.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:58.530
But it was completely meaningless
to visit that location so many times.

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:03.870
Because the location where I ran over
Naganawa wasn't D Hill, but C Hill.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:10.040
I ran over Naganawa with gusto at C Hill,
and then stuffed her into the trunk.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.710
Then transported her to the
crosswalk at D Hill.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.380
By the way, Dojima...

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.920
The reason why I'm telling you this right now

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:24.010
is so that right before your speech, you can't
rely on help from your handsome friends

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:28.350
and I can make you feel uneasy
so my chances of winning increase.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:29.390
Do you get it?

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.770
You... What are you?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:43.280
I'm an "ordinary middle school student
you'd find anywhere, with no redeeming values."

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:48.950
I live a mediocre life, do mediocrely well
in school, and have mediocre athletic abilities.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.460
Liked and disliked mediocrely, too.
And then...

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:58.300
...mediocrely kill people off
in a spur of the moment.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:02.930
Was someone like this in my class?

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.850
No, there wasn't.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.020
There definitely wasn't.

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:12.600
There was no student
named Kinshiro Yokuya in Class 2-B.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.770
Of course I'd feel something was off.
Of course he's un-individualistic.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.900
He's an aggregate of a middle school student.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:22.280
He's not mediocre. He's average.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:26.580
A character that just gathered everything
that defined a male middle school student,

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:32.000
In order to become student council president,
he put on an airs like he'd always been around,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.420
and before anyone realized it,
he was taking classes in 2-B.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.630
Oh, so you can still stand.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:46.180
You have more guts than I thought.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.600
I'm surprised.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:52.100
I should have properly ran over
you back then.

00:12:54.730 --> 00:12:59.270
I honestly felt
that I was glad it was just only me.

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:03.570
Those good-natured boys do not need to know
about this poisonous fang.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:09.490
But either way, you won't win the election.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:17.210
Those poll results were simply a sampling
of honest students answering sluggish questions.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.960
That's not where I can
showcase my true abilities.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.880
My shadow won't shine.

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:24.420
What do you mean?

00:13:24.420 --> 00:13:27.550
I'm saying that a majority
of the students are like me.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:31.520
I had expected that you
were on this side, too.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:37.480
Like polls, signature collections,
and well... Politics and ideals?

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:41.570
Things like that are all cumbersome,
and can't help but feel so weary.

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.740
But they're not so against
the organization enough to revolt,

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:47.870
so they all gather here when they're told to.

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:52.580
People like that are my supporters.
They're my allies.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:56.500
They choose people like them.
They choose the more easy-going guy.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:01.550
Those people talking on stage right now
don't realize that.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:04.800
The more you look down on the audience
and talk about your ideals,

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:08.760
the more we think,
"We can't keep up with all this."

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:14.770
You came to a pretty good position,
but it's the end for you right here.

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:20.980
When the current student council president gives
his speech, that's when your defeat is decided.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:24.610
It's one thing
if you were supporting them secretly,

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:28.450
but when people with power
come on stage, it's all over.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:32.740
Then you'll be categorized as "one of them,"
someone on a different level.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:37.330
Just like me, you should've asked a "friend you
feel amiable with" for the campaign speech

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:40.290
instead of someone from the privileged class.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.420
I don't have any friends I feel amiable with.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.880
What I have...

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:54.140
Next, we have the endorsement speech
for Mayumi Dojima.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.060
Nagahiro Sakiguchi, please go ahead.

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.500
Ladies and gentlemen, lend an ear!

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:27.970
"ENDORSEMENT SPEECH"

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.050
Ladies and gentlemen, lend an ear!

00:15:32.140 --> 00:15:33.470
Just kidding.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:38.850
Of course, as you can see, I'm not Nagahiro, the
Student Council President Nagahiro Sakiguchi.

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:41.480
I asked him for a huge favor
to let me go up instead.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:47.360
It's because I wanted to support
Mayumi no matter what.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:50.650
Can you understand
how I'm feeling right now?

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:54.990
This is a speech, an endorsement speech,
for you to understand that.

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:02.420
However, it's not like I want to support her
to become student council president.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:09.300
If that sounds bad, I will correct that to say,
"I want to cheer for everything Mayumi does."

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:14.140
And if possible,
I'd like all of you to support her as well.

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:20.230
The first time I saw her
was on the rooftop on campus.

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.940
She was a girl who searched for a star.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:28.780
She kept searching all this time for a Dark Star
that she only saw once ten years ago.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:30.940
Even when she was denied
that "such a thing doesn't exist,"

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.450
"PLAYING GAMES WILL STOP
AT YOUR SECOND YEAR OF MIDDLE SCHOOL."
even if she lost the recognition
from those around her,

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:40.660
she stubbornly and obstinately
kept looking up at the stars.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.370
I thought she was beautiful for doing so.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.750
I thought that from the bottom of my heart.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:52.130
Those eyes that continued
to single-mindedly look up at the skies.

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:56.720
In the end, such a star
did not exist anywhere in the night sky,

00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:01.310
but that didn't cause
her two eyes to lose their brilliance.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:05.100
Following one's dream is beautiful.

00:17:05.100 --> 00:17:09.820
But giving up on it is similarly beautiful.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:13.570
Mayumi Dojima continued
to sparkle like the stars.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:19.120
One time, she got a hold
of a large sum of money.

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:22.830
A wad of bills suddenly jumped into
her possession without any reason.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:29.920
As it turns out, she did not take advantage of
the fortune that unexpectedly fell into her lap.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:34.050
It was likely moral sense,
and also likely to be moral values.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:37.850
Perhaps it's correct to call it self-control.

00:17:37.850 --> 00:17:43.140
But I would like to think
that her actions were based on self-respect.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:47.400
Not self-control to be just,
but self-respect to be beautiful.

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:50.690
She's not perfect, either.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:55.950
She seems to have deeply angered
one of her friends.

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.700
It would've been great
if I could introduce that episode

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:03.750
and say that in the end, she admitted
she was wrong and honestly apologized.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:07.040
But I heard that Mayumi never apologized.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:11.960
She didn't show it with an apology that were
only words, but demonstrated it with results.

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:18.050
That aspect can't really be applauded
all the time, but there's no need to worry.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:22.140
Where she lacks, we will be supporting her.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:26.640
Just like how she supports us
when we're lacking.

00:18:28.850 --> 00:18:35.440
Of course, she's not like a character who practices
nepotism and only cherishes her allies.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:41.450
As proof, she saved a heel
that she hated and who hated her back.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:46.120
She knew that she wouldn't be appreciated,
and knew that she'll be ostracized for it.

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:49.750
That was something not even I
could do.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:18:54.420
We all love Mayumi.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:58.880
So if she's giving her best effort,
we'll fully support her with everything we have.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:03.600
If Mayumi became student council president,
I'm sure it'll be fun and amusing.

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:09.390
She's not perfect,
so I'm sure she'll make mistakes.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.520
She'll definitely become
stuck-up at times.

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:17.070
But if that happens, I promise you
that we'll give her a harsh scolding.

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:24.080
Just like how she was seriously angry at me
when I was about to become disheartened.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:28.040
Because we are a team.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.790
We will become who she wants us to be.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:40.550
However, if we have one complaint about her,
it's that her self-evaluation is ridiculously low.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:43.970
Even now, she thinks
she's a substitute candidate

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.470
who had no choice but to
begrudgingly enter the election.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.060
Even if she were elected,

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:53.770
she'll think it's because of the support
from the current student council president.

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:55.520
I don't like that.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.820
That's why I want you to teach her.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:01.360
That everyone here has discerning eyes.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.410
Not tricked by superficial or back-end ideas,

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:08.000
and not fooled by lip service or by ideals.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.500
You can see the actual person.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:14.460
You can see the actual truth.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.210
Let's show her what we can do.

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:23.050
If you had already chosen a candidate, so be it.

00:20:23.050 --> 00:20:26.260
You can forget about
my "bragging" as well.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.640
This might be strange to say,

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:33.060
but once voting is over, please visit Mayumi
when she returns to being an ordinary student.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:37.610
See her, talk to her,
and please become friends with her.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.070
That will be all!

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:41.530
North to south!

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:45.660
"EPILOGUE"

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.080
"ART ROOM"

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.080
Mayumi Dojima from Class 2-B

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:49.120
Mayumi Dojima from Class 2-B

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:53.370
has been triumphant, and was elected
as the next student council president.

00:20:59.090 --> 00:21:02.720
In the end, who exactly was that guy?

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:08.010
You said he wasn't a student of Yubiwa
Academy, let alone your classmate.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:15.770
A reasonable train of thought is an assassin
from the academy to slim down the curriculum.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:18.690
It's not that scary, but it's sure chaotic.

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:21.320
It's like, you'd really go that far?

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:25.740
In any case, there are many things
Miss Mayumi needs to be careful for

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:29.120
while running the student council.

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.910
It's only going to be uphill from here.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:37.290
I didn't need be told that,
but after such support from our leader,

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:41.550
as well as being shown
just how many people had voted for me,

00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:44.010
I have no time to be saying things like that.

00:21:44.010 --> 00:21:50.010
I can't have people who believed in me think,
"I didn't have an eye for character."

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:55.020
Scum may be scum, but I'm going to be
the celestial scum that glimmers, like stardust.

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:58.560
I'm going to shine, even in the light.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:02.110
--Nagahiro, can you show me
that sash more closely?
--In a few more months,
Mr. Senpai will be gone from middle school.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:03.320
--Stop it, my leader.
This is quite embarrassing.
--In a few more months,
Mr. Senpai will be gone from middle school.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:05.650
--Stop it, my leader.
This is quite embarrassing.
--Even the fifth grader
won't be a fifth grader forever.

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:06.860
--Is that so? That looks really good on you,
former student council president.
--Even the fifth grader
won't be a fifth grader forever.

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:09.030
--Is that so? That looks really good on you,
former student council president.
--And as for me, I can't gaze
downward forever.

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.910
--So Michiru, were you able
to mend fences with Sosaku?
--And as for me, I can't gaze
downward forever.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:15.210
--It's not like we were arguing.
--We weren't.
--Someday, that night sky that I've been
averting my eyes from quite a while ago...

00:22:15.210 --> 00:22:16.670
--Someday, that night sky that I've been
averting my eyes from quite a while ago...

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.040
"MAYUMI NEW STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENT"
"FORMER STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENT"

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:21.040
I can't stay as-is.

00:22:21.420 --> 00:22:26.970
In the past, I used to go to school
dressed up like a boy.

00:22:26.970 --> 00:22:31.140
I used to make food at school every day.

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:32.680
I used to be ridiculed as a lolicon,

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:36.480
and dedicated myself to a grade school
child with a soft coaxing tone.

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:40.560
I spent all year in shorts.

00:22:40.560 --> 00:22:44.650
Back then, I assumed I was a silent artist.

00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:48.740
I used to play detective and learned from it.

00:22:48.740 --> 00:22:53.700
Just like that, so we can talk about the past
with a few implications,

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:58.040
we must live today
so that it can someday become a memory.

00:22:58.960 --> 00:23:03.170
We must live beautifully.

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:07.720
My boys, do you all have some orange juice
that Michiru squeezed for us?

00:23:07.720 --> 00:23:12.550
Well then, let's have a toast
to celebrate Mayumi's beautiful victory.

00:23:12.550 --> 00:23:13.810
Cowabunga!

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:18.100
Cheers to the irreplaceable present.

00:23:18.100 --> 00:23:19.940
To the present that is only here now.

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:22.730
To now being the time.
